From 54ea902ae7f3a3c12a420802cf0b1e79665b531c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:13:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/31] android: Build the software ISP IPA for the Exynos 7870
 CSIS

The Android build files do not build the IPA module of the software
ISP: without it IPAManager::createIPA() fails, and a raw Bayer sensor
behind a simple pipeline receiver gives no camera.

- Build ipa_soft_simple and ship it in the camera provider APEX, with
  IPA_MODULE_DIR pointing there, and install the uncalibrated tuning
  file in /vendor/etc/libcamera/ipa/simple.
- On Android, without a signing key, trust the IPA modules found in
  IPA_MODULE_DIR instead of isolating them in a proxy worker that is
  not installed.
- Add the Exynos 7870 CSIS to the simple pipeline handler, with the
  software ISP.
- Add a camera sensor helper for the SK hynix SR259: linear gain in
  1/16 steps, black level of 64 at 10 bits.
- Link libyaml and libyuv statically, as AOSP's external/libcamera
  does, move the cam binary to the root package where libyaml is
  visible, and stop redefining _FORTIFY_SOURCE.

Assisted-by: LLM
